            <ArticleTitle>Reprogramming Tumor Blood Vessels for Enhancing Immunotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>809-812</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2405-8033(17)30196-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.trecan.2017.10.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiogenic blood vessels contribute to generating an immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment, in part by limiting the extravasation of T cells. Functional reprogramming of angiogenic blood vessels, for example through angiopoietin-2 blockade, may improve T cell trafficking in tumors and the efficacy of immune checkpoint blockade (ICB) and other cancer immunotherapies.</AbstractText>
